u-boot-gemini-simplefb (2026.10.2+twostage.74977014574) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Stage-2 chainload hardening (review round 2): arm the RGU watchdog before
    booti and enable CONFIG_WATCHDOG so a hung stage 2 self-resets; refuse to
    chainload if the boot counter did not persist (PMIC/RTC fail-open); tag the
    stage-2 kernel command line with gemini_stage=2 as a chainload discriminator.

 -- realni <ant@ict4.cz>  Mon, 27 Oct 2026 15:00:00 +0000

u-boot-gemini-simplefb (2026.10.2+twostage.2e40f8aaed7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Loop guard for the stage-2 chainload: count each chainload attempt against
    "bootlimit" and drop to fastboot once exceeded, so a stage 2 that hangs
    before Linux clears the RTC boot counter can no longer loop forever. Reset
    rather than resume stage 1 if booti ever returns after relocation.

 -- realni <ant@ict4.cz>  Mon, 27 Oct 2026 13:00:00 +0000

u-boot-gemini-simplefb (2026.10.2+twostage.fdbdffa43e8) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Two-stage boot. Stage 1 (flashed once into the write-protected "boot"
    partition) chainloads a verified stage-2 U-Boot from
    /boot/u-boot/u-boot-stage2.img on the "linux" partition before the
    bootmenu, so U-Boot updates become plain file writes. The stage-2 image is
    built from the same tree with the chainload disabled (loop guard) and
    shipped alongside with its sha256 digest. Any failure or a held key falls
    back to stage 1 (bootmenu, bootfallback, fastboot, extlinux).

 -- realni <ant@ict4.cz>  Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000

u-boot-gemini-simplefb (2026.10.1+bootfallback.d3585b753b7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Always power on the Cortex-A72 cluster and stop injecting maxcpus into
    the kernel command line; all ten CPUs now come up with a plain cmdline.
    On a power-on failure the A72 cpu nodes are marked "fail" in the DT so
    Linux skips them.

 -- realni <ant@ict4.cz>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 20:00:00 +0000

u-boot-gemini-simplefb (2026.10+bootfallback.f3e24215628) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Drop the TOPRGU WDT-status gate (the preloader clears the latch, so it
    reset the streak every cycle and the device WDT-looped). U-Boot now only
    increments; Linux clears the count on a good boot. Same artifacts.

 -- realni <ant@ict4.cz>  Sat, 25 Oct 2026 15:00:00 +0000

u-boot-gemini-simplefb (2026.10+bootfallback.d10bc8dbe70) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix the fallback being inert: bake bootlimit=3 and altbootcmd into the
    compiled default env (CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_BOOTLIMIT / _ALTBOOTCMD) instead of
    board_late_init env_set, which env_default.h shadowed. Same artifacts.

 -- realni <ant@ict4.cz>  Sat, 25 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000

u-boot-gemini-simplefb (2026.10+bootfallback.cc819dcbb6f) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Boot-failure fallback variant (tip cc819dcbb6f, on top of the charger
    build): CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_LIMIT counts consecutive RGU watchdog resets in
    the always-on MT6351 RTC and runs "fastboot usb 0" once the count exceeds
    bootlimit, so a hung cold boot recovers without the side button. Same
    artifacts.

 -- realni <ant@ict4.cz>  Sat, 25 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000

